export default function Page2(){return <><Frame0 /><main><section id={"ss-page-head"} className={"custom-ph"} aria-labelledby={"ss-page-title"}><div className={"custom-hero-photo custom-ph-photo absolute inset-0 -z-1 overflow-hidden"} style={{"--custom-pos": "72% 40%"}}><img className={"size-full object-cover object-[var(--custom-pos,50%_50%)]"} src={"https://draftmango.com/framo/assets/media/placeholder/2400x1350.svg"} alt={"A security tester working through code on two monitors late in the evening"} width={"2400"} height={"1350"} fetchPriority={"high"} decoding={"async"} /></div><div className={"container custom-ph-content"}><nav className={"custom-ph-crumb mb-6 text-[0.9375rem]"} aria-label={"Breadcrumb"} data-anim={"fade"} data-anim-duration={"800"}><ol className={"breadcrumb"}><li className={"breadcrumb-item"}><a href={"#page=demo-security-services-1"}>{"Home"}</a></li><li className={"breadcrumb-item"}><a href={"#page=demo-security-services-1-research"}>{"Research"}</a></li><li className={"breadcrumb-item"} aria-current={"page"}>{"Push Fatigue Is Back"}</li></ol></nav><p className={"custom-hero-tag mb-6"} data-anim={"fade-up"}>{"Identity · Field note"}</p><h1 id={"ss-page-title"} className={"custom-ph-title max-w-[15ch] text-[clamp(2.75rem,1.5rem_+_4vw,5.5rem)] font-bold leading-[0.98] tracking-[-0.045em] text-white text-balance"} data-anim={"fade-up"} data-anim-delay={"80"} data-anim-duration={"1100"}>{"Push fatigue is back: how we got past MFA "}<em className={"custom-serif font-serif"}>{"four times."}</em></h1><p className={"custom-ph-meta flex flex-wrap gap-y-1 gap-x-5 mt-6 text-[1rem]"} data-anim={"fade-up"} data-anim-delay={"200"}><span>{"Identity"}</span><span>{"Oct 7, 2026"}</span><span>{"6 min read"}</span><span>{"By Nora Lindgren"}</span></p></div></section><section id={"ss-article"} className={"custom-section custom-article"} aria-label={"Article"}><div className={"container"}><article className={"article-body px-0"}><p className={"text-[clamp(1.375rem,1.2rem_+_0.6vw,1.75rem)] leading-[1.45] tracking-[-0.015em] text-text"}>{"Four times this year, on four different clients, the same trick got our red team past multi-factor authentication. None of it needed malware. All of it needed a tired person and a phone."}</p><p>{"Push-based MFA was meant to end the stolen-password problem, and for the most part it did. But a push prompt asks a single question — "}<em>{"was this you?"}</em>{" — and people answer questions to make them go away. Send enough of them at the right hour and someone says yes."}</p><p>{"Here's what those four engagements looked like, what stopped us on a fifth, and the three changes we now recommend to every client on push MFA."}</p><h2>{"What we found"}</h2><p>{"In each case we started with a password from an old breach list or a convincing login page. The second factor was the only thing left in the way."}</p><div className={"custom-article-findings overflow-hidden bg-(--custom-paper) border border-(--custom-line) rounded-(--custom-radius-card)"}><p className={"flex justify-between gap-4 py-4 px-5 text-[0.9375rem] font-semibold text-text"}><span>{"Findings across four red team engagements"}</span><span className={"custom-small"}>{"2026"}</span></p><ol role={"list"}><li className={"custom-finding custom-finding--critical"}><span className={"custom-finding-sev"}>{"Critical"}</span><span className={"custom-finding-title"}>{"Push prompt approved after repeated requests"}</span><span className={"custom-finding-cvss"}>{"9.1"}</span><span className={"custom-finding-status custom-finding-status--fixed"}>{"Fixed"}</span></li><li className={"custom-finding custom-finding--high"}><span className={"custom-finding-sev"}>{"High"}</span><span className={"custom-finding-title"}>{"No number matching on the authenticator"}</span><span className={"custom-finding-cvss"}>{"8.0"}</span><span className={"custom-finding-status custom-finding-status--fixed"}>{"Fixed"}</span></li><li className={"custom-finding custom-finding--high"}><span className={"custom-finding-sev"}>{"High"}</span><span className={"custom-finding-title"}>{"No alert on a burst of denied prompts"}</span><span className={"custom-finding-cvss"}>{"7.2"}</span><span className={"custom-finding-status custom-finding-status--fixed"}>{"Fixed"}</span></li><li className={"custom-finding custom-finding--medium"}><span className={"custom-finding-sev"}>{"Medium"}</span><span className={"custom-finding-title"}>{"Sign-ins allowed from any country"}</span><span className={"custom-finding-cvss"}>{"5.3"}</span><span className={"custom-finding-status text-(--custom-alert)"}>{"Open"}</span></li></ol></div><h2>{"Why it still works"}</h2><p>{"Timing does most of the work. Prompts sent at 11 p.m. or just before the morning stand-up were approved far more often than ones sent mid-afternoon. In one case the approval came after the ninth prompt; in another, after a friendly call from "IT" explaining that the prompts were part of a migration."}</p><figure className={"article-wide"}><img className={"w-full aspect-[21/9] object-cover rounded-(--custom-radius-frame)"} src={"https://draftmango.com/framo/assets/media/placeholder/1800x771.svg"} alt={"A hand on a laptop keyboard lit by a violet screen in the dark"} width={"1800"} height={"771"} loading={"lazy"} /><figcaption className={"mt-3.5 text-[0.9375rem] text-(--custom-meta)"}>{"Most approvals came outside working hours, from people trying to get back to what they were doing."}</figcaption></figure><p>{"On the fifth engagement we didn't get in. That client had turned on number matching, so a prompt meant nothing without the code on the login screen, and their SOC was alerting on bursts of denied pushes. We gave up after two hours."}</p><figure className={"custom-article-quote"}><blockquote className={"text-[clamp(1.75rem,1.3rem_+_1.4vw,2.5rem)] font-bold leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.035em] text-text text-balance"}>{"A push prompt asks one question, and people answer questions "}<em className={"custom-serif font-serif"}>{"to make them go away."}</em></blockquote><figcaption className={"text-[1rem] text-(--custom-meta)"}>{"Nora Lindgren, Senior Red Team Operator"}</figcaption></figure><h2>{"Three changes worth making this week"}</h2><ol><li><strong>{"Turn on number matching."}</strong>{" It's a setting in every major identity provider and it ends blind approvals."}</li><li><strong>{"Alert on denied bursts."}</strong>{" Five denied prompts in ten minutes is an attack, not a mistake."}</li><li><strong>{"Move admins to phishing-resistant keys."}</strong>{" Start with the twenty accounts that would hurt most."}</li></ol><h3>{"The detection we use"}</h3><p>{"If your sign-in logs land in Microsoft Sentinel, this is the query our SOC runs. Adjust the threshold to your noise level."}</p><pre className={"custom-article-code py-5 px-6 text-[0.9375rem] leading-[1.6] text-(--custom-on-ink) bg-(--custom-ink) rounded-(--custom-radius-card)"}><code>{"SigninLogs
| where TimeGenerated > ago(1h)
| where ResultType == "500121"   // MFA denied by user
| summarize Denied = count() by UserPrincipalName, bin(TimeGenerated, 10m)
